INT. AEROSTAT BAKERY - UPPER CLOUD DECK OF VENUS - DAY

A warm, low-ceilinged kitchen suspended in the sulfur haze, its walls lined with copper ovens and rattling racks of dough. Through a thick quartz porthole, orange clouds roil like boiling custard. The air smells of yeast and faint lemon. Every surface is bolted down.

At a floured table kneads MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN, 60s, the head baker, a woman built like a ship's prow, with burn scars freckling her forearms and a gaze that has outlasted three bankruptcies. Beside her, PIETRO, 19, her apprentice, is piping icing onto a tray of tiny cakes with the care of someone defusing a bomb.

An intercom speaker above the oven door crackles.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Bakery, this is Dispatch. Cloud shear in four minutes. Secure your loose items.

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
Acknowledged.

She wipes her hands on her apron. Pietro glances at the porthole, where the clouds are beginning to churn faster. A cake slips from the tray and lands on the floor with a quiet splat.

At the back, NOOR, 30s, a pastry cook with flour to her elbows, hauls a tray of buns into the warming rack and does not turn around.

NOOR
Starboard shutters are down, Madame.

PIETRO
Madame. The shear is on the starboard side.

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
I can smell it.

PIETRO
Should we turn off the ovens?

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
We do not turn off the ovens. We turn off the nerves.

The floor shudders. Racks rattle. A cloud of flour lifts from the table and hangs in the air like smoke. Madame Adebola-Quinn lays a steady hand on a copper oven door. Pietro takes the icing bag in a white-knuckled grip and keeps piping.

The door at the far end of the kitchen bangs open. A figure staggers in, a tall woman in a gray inspector's coat dusted with orange pollen, holding a clipboard and a respirator mask in one hand. This is INSPECTOR LOGANATHAN, 40s, severe, her lenses fogged. She coughs and waves the mask.

INSPECTOR LOGANATHAN
Surprise audit. Nobody move.

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
We are about to be sheared.

INSPECTOR LOGANATHAN
Then this will be a very memorable audit.

The floor drops half a foot, rises again. Everything tilts. Pietro yelps. A rack of rolls crashes to the floor and scatters across the tile. The inspector grabs the nearest table and hangs on.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Shear in thirty seconds. All hands, brace.

PIETRO
(near tears)
I don't want to die in a bakery!

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
(deadpan)
You'll die in a very clean bakery.

INSPECTOR LOGANATHAN
(writing on her clipboard)
That's the first compliment I've noted.

The shear hits. The whole kitchen lurches, spins a quarter turn on its tether, and settles. Flour falls like snow. Then, slowly, the shaking stops. The orange clouds beyond the porthole begin to calm. They stand there, three people covered in white, hanging on to a table.

PIETRO
(tiny)
Did we make it?

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Shear has passed. Carry on.

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN
(to the room)
Carry on.

She straightens. Picks a cake off the floor, blows on it, and bites it. She nods.

MADAME ADEBOLA-QUINN (CONT'D)
Still good.

The inspector lowers her clipboard. She takes a cake from the tray, tastes it, and lowers her mask.

INSPECTOR LOGANATHAN
Pass.
